WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:06.140
In 2006, a large study in the United States
followed patients after heart surgery.

2
00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.870
Some of them were prayed for.

3
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.230
Others were not.

4
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.250
Would it make any difference?

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.600
Every day, millions of people
pray: alone or together,

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.880
in set words or their own.

7
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.110
Some say their prayers were answered.

8
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.210
Others prayed hard, and nothing changed.

9
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.890
So if someone prays for
a friend to get better,

10
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.560
and she doesn't, was the
prayer answered at all?

11
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.220
In this mission, you'll explore
four kinds of Christian prayer,

12
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.450
and read what the First
Letter of John promises.

13
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.650
Then you'll weigh up
the critics' challenges,

14
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.310
and hear how Christians reply to them.

15
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.320
Your mission: work out what
counts as an answer to prayer.
